t recent items and open loops that may still matter, flagged as older.\n\nShould I check calendar? The user asked about mailboxes. I''ll offer. Actually \"what needs my attention\" — a quick calendar check could add value but the question is scoped to mailboxes. I''ll keep it to mail and offer calendar.\n\nLet me write the answer."}],"createdAt":1794331769024},{"type":"text","text":"**1 mailbox** — nothing arrived this week.\n\n## ana@demo.trymetis.email\nNo mail at all in the window Mon 2 Nov – Fri 6 Nov 2026. Also zero unread and zero starred messages in the whole mailbox.\n\nThe newest message in the inbox is from **Sat 26 Sep 2026** — six weeks ago — so the mailbox has been quiet since then, not just this week.\n\n**Last activity, for context (all September, all read):**\n- **Raj Mehta** — *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC* — that meeting date has now passed.\n- **Raj Mehta** — *Updated invitation: Aozora logo review (internal) @ Thu Oct 1, 2026 14:00 UTC* — also past.\n- **Northbeam Air** — *Schedule change for booking NB7Q4K* — a travel change you may want to confirm was handled.\n- **Linkroom** — *Your Linkroom Pro plan renews on October 3* — renewal date has passed; worth checking it billed as expected.\n- **Konkan Bank** — *INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821* — routine debit.\n\nTwo things worth flagging: the two meeting invitations above are the only items that ever needed a response, and both dates are behind us. And a six-week gap in a connected IMAP inbox can mean the connection has stopped syncing rather than that you genuinely received nothing — if you were expecting mail, that''s worth verifying.\n\nWant me to check your calendars for what''s actually on this week, or look at a specific thread from September?","createdAt":1794331769024}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**1 mailbox** — nothing arrived this week.\n\n## ana@demo.trymetis.email\nNo mail at 