INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('7f322445-c9b4-4216-a9ce-58086188cf8f','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"- **What it is** — the Aozora Ceramics rebrand brief, written by client brand manager **Kenji Watanabe** for Fernhill Studio, aimed at design-led cafes, restaurants and home cooks in Japan and Europe.\n- **What''s owed** — a wordmark and mark (**three options at the first review**), a colour and type system, and packaging for mugs, plates and the gift box; budget **JPY 1,850,000**, with one hard constraint: *\"Keep the colour blue somewhere. It has been on every Aozora cup since 1962.\"*\n- **When** — kickoff 2026-10-05, first review 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC (both now past), and **final files due 2026-11-20** — 10 days from today and the only outstanding deadline.","createdAt":1794331927576}],"content":"- **What it is** — the Aozora Ceramics rebrand brief, written by client brand manager **Kenji Watanabe** for Fernhill Studio, aimed at design-led cafes, restaurants and home cooks in Japan and Europe.\n- **What''s owed** — a wordmark and mark (**three options at the first review**), a colour and type system, and packaging for mugs, plates and the gift box; budget **JPY 1,850,000**, with one hard constraint: *\"Keep the colour blue somewhere. It has been on every Aozora cup since 1962.\"*\n- **When** — kickoff 2026-10-05, first review 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC (both now past), and **final files due 2026-11-20** — 10 days from today and the only outstanding deadline.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:07.576Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('82368b69-904d-4d61-bc72-224348505174','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-10T17:32:07.591Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1794331927597},{"type":"text","text":"Does the brief mention the same deadline as the kickoff email?","createdAt":1794331927597}]}','user','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:07.611Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('847d9f5f-90fd-4caf-8f11-86326dbe62cd','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Question: \"Does the brief mention the same deadline as the kickoff email?\"\n\nKickoff email (Raj, 21 Sep): \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5. Can you send me the moodboard by Friday, and confirm whether Tomás can join the first review?\" — deadlines: moodboard by Friday (25 Sep), rebrand start Oct 5.\n\nBrief: kickoff 2026-10-05, first review 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC, final files 2026-11-20.\n\nOverlap: the kickoff date Oct 5 agrees in both. The brief''s \"final files 20 Nov\" doesn''t appear in the kickoff email. And the email''s moodboard-by-Friday deadline doesn''t appear in the brief. So partial overlap only — they agree on the 5 Oct start; the email has no \"final files\" date, and the brief has no moodboard date.\n\nShould I double-check the kickoff email again? I have it verbatim from turn 1. And there may be other rebrand emails with deadlines (the Aozora review agenda from Raj 19 Sep, the Rebrand review invite 24 Sep at 15:00–15:45). The invite email''s time matched the brief''s first review time. But the question is specifically about the kickoff email.\n\nAnswer precisely: Yes and no — the only date they share is the 5 Oct kickoff. Be clear about the mismatch. Also mention \"Friday\" nuance: the email was sent Mon 21 Sep 2026; Friday = 25 Sep.\n\nKeep concise.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Question: \"Does the brief mention the same deadline as the kickoff email?\"\n\nKickoff email (Raj, 21 Sep): \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5. Can you send me the moodboard by Friday, and confirm whether Tomás can join the first review?\" — deadlines: moodboard by Friday (25 Sep), rebrand start Oct 5.\n\nBrief: kickoff 2026-10-05, first review 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC, final files 2026-11-20.\n\nOverlap: the kickoff date Oct 5 agrees in both. The brief''s \"final files 20 Nov\" doesn''t appear in the kickoff email. And the email''s moodboard-by-Friday deadline doesn''t appear in the brief. So partial overlap only — they agree on the 5 Oct start; the email has no \"final files\" date, and the brief has no moodboard date.\n\nShould I double-check the kickoff email again? I have it verbatim from turn 1. And there may be other rebrand emails with deadlines (the Aozora review agenda from Raj 19 Sep, the Rebrand review invite 24 Sep at 15:00–15:45). The invite email''s time matched the brief''s first review time. But the question is specifically about the kickoff email.\n\nAnswer precisely: Yes and no — the only date they share is the 5 Oct kickoff. Be clear about the mismatch. Also mention \"Friday\" nuance: the email was sent Mon 21 Sep 2026; Friday = 25 Sep.\n\nKeep concise."}],"createdAt":1794331936909},{"type":"text","text":"Partly — they share exactly one date, and neither contains the other''s other deadlines.\n\n| Milestone | Kickoff email (Raj, 21 Sep) | Brief (Kenji) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Moodboard | **\"by Friday\"** → Fri 25 Sep 2026 | not mentioned |\n| Kickoff / start | **5 Oct 2026** (\"we agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\") | **2026-10-05** ✅ same |\n| First review | mentioned only as \"the first review\", no date | **2026-10-08 15:00 UTC** |\n| Final files | not mentioned | **2026-11-20** |\n\nSo they agree on the **5 Oct start** — the one milestone both state, and the brief''s date matches the email''s exactly. But the brief carries **no moodboard deadline**, and the kickoff email carries **no final-files deadline** (it doesn''t even date the first review).\n\nNet effect: the **20 Nov final-files date exists only in the brief**, and the **25 Sep moodboard date exists only in Raj''s email** — neither document corroborates the other on those two. The first review''s real time (8 Oct, 15:00 UTC) is confirmed elsewhere: by Raj''s separate invitation email and by the *Design review* event on the Work calendar, not by the kickoff email.","createdAt":1794331936909}],"content":"Partly — they share exactly one date, and neither contains the other''s other deadlines.\n\n| Milestone | Kickoff email (Raj, 21 Sep) | Brief (Kenji) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Moodboard | **\"by Friday\"** → Fri 25 Sep 2026 | not mentioned |\n| Kickoff / start | **5 Oct 2026** (\"we agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\") | **2026-10-05** ✅ same |\n| First review | mentioned only as \"the first review\", no date | **2026-10-08 15:00 UTC** |\n| Final files | not mentioned | **2026-11-20** |\n\nSo they agree on the **5 Oct start** — the one milestone both state, and the brief''s date matches the email''s exactly. But the brief carries **no moodboard deadline**, and the kickoff email carries **no final-files deadline** (it doesn''t even date the first review).\n\nNet effect: the **20 Nov final-files date exists only in the brief**, and the **25 Sep moodboard date exists only in Raj''s email** — neither document corroborates the other on those two. The first review''s real time (8 Oct, 15:00 UTC) is confirmed elsewhere: by Raj''s separate invitation email and by the *Design review* event on the Work calendar, not by the kickoff email.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:16.909Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('e2e573cb-f499-42e1-9d85-013c5f825aaf','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-10T17:32:16.923Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1794331936929},{"type":"text","text":"What else is on my calendar on the day of the review?","createdAt":1794331936929}]}','user','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:16.945Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('4ef584c8-9029-4c55-9159-7d2f616e644b','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The review is Thu 8 Oct 2026. From the earlier full list, events on 8 Oct:\n\n- 09:00–09:15 UTC Daily standup — Work\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily forever — Edge cases (a fixture/noise)\n- 10:00–13:00 Workshop: packaging prototypes — Work, Studio 2 (ana, raj, priya)\n- 13:00–13:30 Print vendor call (Pune) — Work (priya)\n- 15:00–16:00 Design review — Work, Studio 2 (the rebrand review)\n- Anything on Personal? 8 Oct — no personal events listed (dentist was 7 Oct 17:00).\n- Also the \"aozora\" query — nothing else.\n\nWait — was there anything else on 8 Oct? Let me re-scan the 2026-10-08 entries in the sweep:\n\n1. rrule-daily-forever (Edge cases) 09:00–09:15\n2. daily-standup 09:00–09:15 Work\n3. packaging-workshop 10:00–13:00 Work\n4. print-vendor 13:00–13:30 Work\n5. design-review 15:00–16:00 Work\n\nThat''s all I saw for Oct 8. But the sweep was capped at 250 events — but it covered Sep 1 onward chronologically sorted, and reached Nov 13, so Oct 8 was fully covered within the cap. Yes: entries ran continuously, so Oct 8 is complete. Good.\n\nShould I verify with a targeted listEvents for Oct 8? The sweep is complete for that date since it sorted by start and included all events between Sep 1 and Nov 13. However, the cap of 250 ended at Nov 13 — Oct 8 was mid-list and fully represented. I''m confident. But a fresh targeted call is cheap and gives certainty... I think the sweep is reliable; no need. Actually, one risk: the sweep was truncated at 250, but truncation drops the tail (later dates), not Oct 8. Fine.\n\nAlso I should mention the Work calendar only; nothing on Personal/Bulk on 8 Oct? Bulk events started Nov 1. Right.\n\nPresent chronologically with times UTC, calendar names. Note Studio 2 double-booking? The packaging workshop is Studio 2 10:00–13:00 and design review Studio 2 15:00–16:00 — not overlapping, fine.\n\nAlso note the back-to-back nature: 15:00 review right after 13:30 end — 90 min gap.\n\nHighlight the day''s shape: workshop ends 13:00, print vendor call 13:00–13:30 (no gap), review at 15:00 — that''s the \"big day\" ending with Studio drinks on Friday.\n\nKeep it scannable.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The review is Thu 8 Oct 2026. From the earlier full list, events on 8 Oct:\n\n- 09:00–09:15 UTC Daily standup — Work\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily forever — Edge cases (a fixture/noise)\n- 10:00–13:00 Workshop: packaging prototypes — Work, Studio 2 (ana, raj, priya)\n- 13:00–13:30 Print vendor call (Pune) — Work (priya)\n- 15:00–16:00 Design review — Work, Studio 2 (the rebrand review)\n- Anything on Personal? 8 Oct — no personal events listed (dentist was 7 Oct 17:00).\n- Also the \"aozora\" query — nothing else.\n\nWait — was there anything else on 8 Oct? Let me re-scan the 2026-10-08 entries in the sweep:\n\n1. rrule-daily-forever (Edge cases) 09:00–09:15\n2. daily-standup 09:00–09:15 Work\n3. packaging-workshop 10:00–13:00 Work\n4. print-vendor 13:00–13:30 Work\n5. design-review 15:00–16:00 Work\n\nThat''s all I saw for Oct 8. But the sweep was capped at 250 events — but it covered Sep 1 onward chronologically sorted, and reached Nov 13, so Oct 8 was fully covered within the cap. Yes: entries ran continuously, so Oct 8 is complete. Good.\n\nShould I verify with a targeted listEvents for Oct 8? The sweep is complete for that date since it sorted by start and included all events between Sep 1 and Nov 13. However, the cap of 250 ended at Nov 13 — Oct 8 was mid-list and fully represented. I''m confident. But a fresh targeted call is cheap and gives certainty... I think the sweep is reliable; no need. Actually, one risk: the sweep was truncated at 250, but truncation drops the tail (later dates), not Oct 8. Fine.\n\nAlso I should mention the Work calendar only; nothing on Personal/Bulk on 8 Oct? Bulk events started Nov 1. Right.\n\nPresent chronologically with times UTC, calendar names. Note Studio 2 double-booking? The packaging workshop is Studio 2 10:00–13:00 and design review Studio 2 15:00–16:00 — not overlapping, fine.\n\nAlso note the back-to-back nature: 15:00 review right after 13:30 end — 90 min gap.\n\nHighlight the day''s shape: workshop ends 13:00, print vendor call 13:00–13:30 (no gap), review at 15:00 — that''s the \"big day\" ending with Studio drinks on Friday.\n\nKeep it scannable."}],"createdAt":1794331958065},{"type":"text","text":"Thu **8 Oct 2026** was a five-event day, all on the **Work** calendar (nothing on Personal, Bulk or Edge cases bar one noise fixture):\n\n- **09:00–09:15 UTC — Daily standup** (Work, linkroom.app/r/standup)\n- **09:00–09:15 UTC — \"Daily forever\"** (Edge cases) — the recurring test fixture sitting on top of your standup, not a real meeting\n- **10:00–13:00 UTC — Workshop: packaging prototypes** (Work, Studio 2) — you + raj@ + priya@\n- **13:00–13:30 UTC — Print vendor call (Pune)** (Work, linkroom.app/r/print-vendor) — priya@\n- **15:00–16:00 UTC — Design review** (Work, Studio 2) — *this is the rebrand review*\n\nShape of the day: a three-hour packaging workshop running straight into the print-vendor call with **no break at 13:00**, then a 90-minute gap before the review at 15:00.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **The review sits 90 minutes after the vendor call and two hours after the workshop ends** — so the packaging workshop was in the same room (Studio 2) five hours ahead of the review. If the workshop output was meant to feed the review, it was same-day.\n2. **The print vendor call is where the 20 Nov final-files date gets real** — a Pune vendor''s turnaround is the likely constraint on that deadline, and it''s the only other production-related event on the day.","createdAt":1794331958065}],"content":"Thu **8 Oct 2026** was a five-event day, all on the **Work** calendar (nothing on Personal, Bulk or Edge cases bar one noise fixture):\n\n- **09:00–09:15 UTC — Daily standup** (Work, linkroom.app/r/standup)\n- **09:00–09:15 UTC — \"Daily forever\"** (Edge cases) — the recurring test fixture sitting on top of your standup, not a real meeting\n- **10:00–13:00 UTC — Workshop: packaging prototypes** (Work, Studio 2) — you + raj@ + priya@\n- **13:00–13:30 UTC — Print vendor call (Pune)** (Work, linkroom.app/r/print-vendor) — priya@\n- **15:00–16:00 UTC — Design review** (Work, Studio 2) — *this is the rebrand review*\n\nShape of the day: a three-hour packaging workshop running straight into the print-vendor call with **no break at 13:00**, then a 90-minute gap before the review at 15:00.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **The review sits 90 minutes after the vendor call and two hours after the workshop ends** — so the packaging workshop was in the same room (Studio 2) five hours ahead of the review. If the workshop output was meant to feed the review, it was same-day.\n2. **The print vendor call is where the 20 Nov final-files date gets real** — a Pune vendor''s turnaround is the likely constraint on that deadline, and it''s the only other production-related event on the day.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:38.065Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
