ation followed. Prior cycle: A-38 ordered 30 Jul, shipped by Swiftpost 1 Aug, out for delivery 4 Aug 06:30, delivered 4 Aug 11:20. For A-42: no Swiftpost notice at all. So ~7 weeks with no tracking email — flag as anomaly, not assertion of loss (maybe spam folder filtering, or the notice went elsewhere).\n\nNothing newer than 23 Sep. Today is 10 Nov. So \"recently\" — the most recent shipment is 48 days ago.\n\nAlso note A-31 etc. historical.\n\nAlso the \"Swiftpost return\" thread from Ana Silva (2 Jun 2026) — a personal email about a return; not needed.\n\nFormat: lead with headline. Include exact dates and mailbox. Mention uncertainty about delivery.\n\nTable maybe. Keep tight."}],"createdAt":1794331989921},{"type":"text","text":"Yes — one, and it''s older than you''d probably expect.\n\n**Headline:** the most recent shipment in your workspace is **Brightloom order A-42, shipped Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC** — that''s **48 days ago**. Nothing has shipped since.\n\nWorkspace has a single mailbox (`ana@demo.trymetis.email`, IMAP), so this is complete coverage — I searched *shipped, order, tracking, dispatch, delivery, Swiftpost* and *A-42* across it.\n\n**Order A-42 cycle** (Brightloom → Swiftpost):\n\n| Step | Date | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| Order placed | Fri 18 Sep 2026, 19:02 UTC | Brightloom — *Thanks for your order A-42* |\n| **Shipped** | **Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC** | Brightloom — *Your order A-42 has shipped* |\n| Carrier pickup | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n| Out for delivery | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n| Delivered | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n\n**The thing that stands out: A-42 never got a delivery confirmation.** Compare the previous cycle, which followed the full pattern — order A-38 placed 30 Jul, Swiftpost *\"on its way\"* 1 Aug, *\"out for delivery today\"* 4 Aug 06:30, *\"delivered\"* 4 Aug 11:20. For A-42 the chain stops dead at \"has shipped\". Seven weeks on, there''s no carrier scan, no delivery, no delay notice (you have received delay notices before — 20 Apr).\n\nTwo caveats before you act on it: the notification could simply not have reached this mailbox, and Brightloom may have used a carrier other than Swiftpost for A-42 — but every other Brightloom order in your mail went through Swiftpost, so that would itself be a change.\n\nOther shipments are all older: A-38 delivered 4 Aug 2026, and delivered parcels back through Apr 2026 and Feb 2025.\n\nWant me to draft a chaser to Brightloom asking for the A-42 tracking number, or check the trashed and spam folders for a delivery notice that got filtered?","createdAt":1794331989921}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"Yes — one, and it''s older than you''d probably expect.\n\n**Headline:** the most recent shipment in your workspace is **Brightloom order A-42, shipped Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC** — that''s **48 days ago**. Nothing has shipped since.\n\nWorkspace has a single mailbox (`ana@demo.trymetis.email`, IMAP), so this is complete coverage — I searched *shipped, order, tracking, dispatch, delivery, Swiftpost* and *A-42* across it.\n\n**Order A-42 cycle** (Brightloom → Swiftpost):\n\n| Step | Date | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| Order placed | Fri 18 Sep 2026, 19:02 UTC | Brightloom — *Thanks for your order A-42* |\n| **Shipped** | **Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC** | Brightloom — *Your order A-42 has shipped* |\n| Carrier pickup | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n| Out for delivery | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n| Delivered | — | *no Swiftpost email* |\n\n**The thing that stands out: A-42 never got a delivery confirmation.** Compare the previous cycle, which followed the full pattern — order A-38 placed 30 Jul, Swiftpost *\"on its way\"* 1 Aug, *\"out for delivery today\"* 4 Aug 06:30, *\"delivered\"* 4 Aug 11:20. For A-42 the chain stops dead at \"has shipped\". Seven weeks on, there''s no carrier scan, no delivery, no delay notice (you have received delay notices before — 20 Apr).\n\nTwo caveats before you act on it: the notification could simply not have reached this mailbox, and Brightloom may have used a carrier other than Swiftpost for A-42 — but every other Brightloom order in your mail went through Swiftpost, so that would itself be a change.\n\nOther shipments are all older: A-38 delivered 4 Aug 2026, and delivered parcels back through Apr 2026 and Feb 2025.\n\nWant me to draft a chaser to Brightloom asking for the A-42 tracking number, or check the trashed and spam folders for a delivery notice that got filtered?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:32:44.696Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
