PT for Brightloom order A-38: out for delivery . Your driver will arrive between 10:00 and 13:00. Track your parcel"},"toolCallId":"call_09c5163b776f4313af4fa019","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM1OV0"}},"updatedAt":1794332007637},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM2MF0","from":"Swiftpost","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Your Swiftpost parcel was delivered","date":"Tue Aug 04 2026 11:20:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Parcel SP4471920402PT for Brightloom order A-38: delivered . Delivered to your mailbox at 11:16. Track your parcel"},"toolCallId":"call_4061bc5fac414687a63bc629","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM2MF0"}},"updatedAt":1794332007637},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwN10","count":0,"attachments":[]},"toolCallId":"call_52a378783ee64d8e85e3eb60","toolName":"listAttachments","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwN10"}},"updatedAt":1794332007637},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794332007639,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now I have the tracking situation:\n\nA-42:\n- Ordered 18 Sep 2026 19:02 UTC. Item: Walnut desk lamp, EUR 129.00, free shipping, total EUR 129.00.\n- Shipped email 23 Sep 2026 10:00 UTC: \"shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30. Track your package\" — **no tracking number at all**. Unlike Swiftpost emails which quote a parcel number.\n- No Swiftpost email for A-42 → no parcel number ever issued in mail.\n- Expected by 30 Sep 2026 → now 41 days past the promised delivery date.\n- No attachments on the shipped email.\n\nNote also: the Brightloom shipped email says \"Track your package\" as a link — but this is a plain-text body; possible link. Hmm, the body came back without a URL. I should mention: the email''s \"Track your package\" link points to Brightloom''s page, but there''s no number. I shouldn''t invent a URL. I''ll just say the mail contains no tracking number and no carrier URL exposed in the text.\n\nA-38 cycle for contrast (all with parcel numbers):\n- 1 Aug: parcel SP4471920368PT shipped, expected Aug 4\n- 4 Aug 06:30: parcel SP4471920385PT out for delivery\n- 4 Aug 11:20: parcel SP4471920402PT delivered to mailbox 11:16\n\nInteresting: three different parcel numbers in one A-38 cycle — SP...368PT, ...385PT, ...402PT. That''s odd (carrier re-issued numbers per scan?). Worth flagging as a detail: the numbers changed between messages, so \"SP4471920xxxPT\" pattern increments. Nothing for A-42 → the sequence jumps: last known ...402PT (4 Aug). No later numbers... hmm, actually we only have 12 Swiftpost emails. Between Aug 4 and now, no Swiftpost emails. So A-42''s shipment generated zero Swiftpost mail.\n\nKey answer: A-42 has NO tracking number anywhere in your mail. And it''s 41 days past the promised 30 Sep.\n\nCompute: 30 Sep → 10 Nov = 41 days. Yes (Sep 30→Oct 30 = 30 days, +11 = 41).\n\nAlso flag: EUR 129 charge — check payment? Not asked. Maybe mention there''s no shipping-fee/tracking issue.\n\nAlso should note: a possible reason no tracking number — Brightloom hand-off never completed; the Swiftpost mail for A-38 came 2 days after ordering though... actually A-38: ordered 30 Jul, Swiftpost on-its-way 1 Aug (1 day later). A-42: shipped email 23 Sep, but no Swiftpost pickup notice ever.\n\nAlso note the Swiftpost return email from Ana Silva 2 Jun 2026 — unrelated.\n\nProvide the tracking verdict clearly, plus what to ask Brightloom for: the parcel number (format SP############PT).\n\nAlso note nothing in trash/spam checked — I could offer. I have no folder-browsing tool loaded... \"one folder of one mailbox\" tool exists per search keywords earlier (\"read... one folder of one mailbox (inbox, sent, drafts, starred, trash, archive, spam)\"). I searched for \"read full email body\" and got getEmail. I could search for \"list emails folder spam archive\" to check trash/spam. But the question is about tracking situation; the mail search already covers all folders? searchMail searches mailboxes — unclear if it includes spam/trash. Likely it searches everything the workspace indexes. To be rigorous, I could check the spam folder for Swiftpost, since a filtered delivery notice would explain the gap. Let me offer rather than do? The user asked specifically \"what is the tracking situation\" — I''ll answer and offer to sweep trash/spam. Actually, being thorough is better: I could search for a listing tool for folders. But that''s another 2 turns. The previous turn I already offered \"check the trashed and spam folders\" and the user instead asked a different question. I''ll answer now and re-offer.\n\nHmm — but maybe there''s a real chance the delivery notice is in spam and the search would miss it. searchMail says \"searches EVERY mailbox by default\", implying it covers the whole mailbox including folders. The delivered notices from April/Feb 2025 came from \"Archive\" folder ids — indeed some results had folder prefix \"Archive\" in the base64 id (WyJBcmNoaXZlIiwiMTAwMCIsODJd → [\"Archive\",\"1000\",82]). So the search does span folders including Archive. Good sign that searchMail is mailbox-wide across folders. So absence is meaningful-ish. I''ll note the caveat that a notice could have been filtered/deleted, and offer the spam/trash sweep.\n\nWrite the answer.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the tracking situation:\n\nA-42:\n- Ordered 18 Sep 2026 19:02 UTC. Item: Walnut desk lamp, EUR 129.00, free shipping, total EUR 129.00.\n- Shipped email 23 Sep 2026 10:00 UTC: \"shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30. Track your package\" — **no tracking number at all**. Unlike Swiftpost emails which quote a parcel number.\n- No Swiftpost email for A-42 → no parcel number ever issued in mail.\n- Expected by 30 Sep 2026 → now 41 days past the promised delivery date.\n- No attachments on the shipped email.\n\nNote also: the Brightloom shipped email says \"Track your package\" as a link — but this is a plain-text body; possible link. Hmm, the body came back without a URL. I should mention: the email''s \"Track your package\" link points to Brightloom''s page, but there''s no number. I shouldn''t invent a URL. I''ll just say the mail contains no tracking number and no carrier URL exposed in the text.\n\nA-38 cycle for contrast (all with parcel numbers):\n- 1 Aug: parcel SP4471920368PT shipped, expected Aug 4\n- 4 Aug 06:30: parcel SP4471920385PT out for delivery\n- 4 Aug 11:20: parcel SP4471920402PT delivered to mailbox 11:16\n\nInteresting: three different parcel numbers in one A-38 cycle — SP...368PT, ...385PT, ...402PT. That''s odd (carrier re-issued numbers per scan?). Worth flagging as a detail: the numbers changed between messages, so \"SP4471920xxxPT\" pattern increments. Nothing for A-42 → the sequence jumps: last known ...402PT (4 Aug). No later numbers... hmm, actually we only have 12 Swiftpost emails. Between Aug 4 and now, no Swiftpost emails. So A-42''s shipment generated zero Swiftpost mail.\n\nKey answer: A-42 has NO tracking number anywhere in your mail. And it''s 41 days past the promised 30 Sep.\n\nCompute: 30 Sep → 10 Nov = 41 days. Yes (Sep 30→Oct 30 = 30 days, +11 = 41).\n\nAlso flag: EUR 129 charge — check payment? Not asked. Maybe mention there''s no shipping-fee/tracking issue.\n\nAlso should note: a possible reason no tracking number — Brightloom hand-off never completed; the Swiftpost mail for A-38 came 2 days after ordering though... actually A-38: ordered 30 Jul, Swiftpost on-its-way 1 Aug (1 day later). A-42: shipped email 23 Sep, but no Swiftpost pickup notice ever.\n\nAlso note the Swiftpost return email from Ana Silva 2 Jun 2026 — unrelated.\n\nProvide the tracking verdict clearly, plus what to ask Brightloom for: the parcel number (format SP############PT).\n\nAlso note nothing in trash/spam checked — I could offer. I have no folder-browsing tool loaded... \"one folder of one mailbox\" tool exists per search keywords earlier (\"read... one folder of one mailbox (inbox, sent, drafts, starred, trash, archive, spam)\"). I searched for \"read full email body\" and got getEmail. I could search for \"list emails folder spam archive\" to check trash/spam. But the question is about tracking situation; the mail search already covers all folders? searchMail searches mailboxes — unclear if it includes spam/trash. Likely it searches everything the workspace indexes. To be rigorous, I could check the spam folder for Swiftpost, since a filtered delivery notice would explain the gap. Let me offer rather than do? The user asked specifically \"what is the tracking situation\" — I''ll answer and offer to sweep trash/spam. Actually, being thorough is better: I could search for a listing tool for folders. But that''s another 2 turns. The previous turn I already offered \"check the trashed and spam folders\" and the user instead asked a different question. I''ll answer now and re-offer.\n\nHmm — but maybe there''s a real chance the delivery notice is in spam and the search would miss it. searchMail says \"searches EVERY mailbox by default\", implying it covers the whole mailbox including folders. The delivered notices from April/Feb 2025 came from \"Archive\" folder ids — indeed some results had folder prefix \"Archive\" in the base64 id (WyJBcmNoaXZlIiwiMTAwMCIsODJd → [\"Archive\",\"1000\",82]). So the search does span folders including Archive. Good sign that searchMail is mailbox-wide across folders. So absence is meaningful-ish. I''ll note the caveat that a notice could have been filtered/deleted, and offer the spam/trash sweep.\n\nWrite the answer."}],"createdAt":1794332032245},{"type":"text","text":"**Tracking situation: there is no tracking number — none was ever issued for A-42.** The parcel number chain simply stops at the order.\n\nWhat the mail actually says:\n\n| | Order A-42 (walnut desk lamp) | Order A-38 (previous, for contrast) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ordered | Fri 18 Sep 2026, 19:02 UTC — EUR 129.00, free shipping | Thu 30 Jul 2026, 18:22 UTC |\n| Shipped notice | Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC — *\"shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30. Track your package\"* | Sat 1 Aug 2026, 07:45 UTC — carrier notice **with number** |\n| **Tracking number** | **none — not in the order email, not in the shipped email, no attachment** | **SP4471920368PT** (Swiftpost) |\n| Out for delivery | — never sent | 4 Aug 06:30 UTC, SP4471920385PT, window 10:00–13:00 |\n| Delivered | — **never sent** | 4 Aug 11:20 UTC, SP4471920402PT, \"delivered to your mailbox at 11:16\" |\n\nThree things stand out:\n\n1. **Brightloom''s shipped email carries no parcel number.** It says the lamp went \"with Swiftpost\" and offers a \"Track your package\" link, but no reference. Every Swiftpost message for A-38 quotes a full number in `SP############PT` form — so the number exists in that system, it just never reached you for A-42.\n2. **The expected date was 30 Sep 2026 — 41 days ago.** That''s the hard failure, not the missing email: the promised delivery passed six weeks back with no delivery, no delay notice (you did get a \"Your parcel is delayed\" notice on 20 Apr, so this isn''t a channel that never fires), and no return-to-sender message. Since the previous cycle went order → Swiftpost pickup in **2 days**, the absence of any carrier handoff mail in 48 days suggests the parcel was never scanned into the network at all.\n3. **Nothing newer exists.** The last Swiftpost number in the whole mailbox is SP4471920402PT on 4 Aug. The numbering looks sequential, so A-42''s would have slotted in after that — there''s no gap message to find, just silence.\n\nSo the practical position: you have a shipped claim dated 23 Sep, a delivery promise of 30 Sep that has expired, and **no evidence in mail that A-42 was ever physically picked up or moved**.\n\nOne caveat: this is everything searchable in the mailbox, spanning inbox and archive. A delivery notice that got filtered into spam and then deleted would be invisible to me — say the word and I''ll sweep trash and spam for Swiftpost directly.\n\nThe chaser to Brightloom writes itself: ask for **the Swiftpost parcel number for order A-42**, and note that the 30 Sep expected date is 41 days past with no delivery and no scan. Want me to draft it?","createdAt":1794332032245}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Tracking situation: there is no tracking number — none was ever issued for A-42.** The parcel number chain simply stops at the order.\n\nWhat the mail actually says:\n\n| | Order A-42 (walnut desk lamp) | Order A-38 (previous, for contrast) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ordered | Fri 18 Sep 2026, 19:02 UTC — EUR 129.00, free shipping | Thu 30 Jul 2026, 18:22 UTC |\n| Shipped notice | Wed 23 Sep 2026, 10:00 UTC — *\"shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30. Track your package\"* | Sat 1 Aug 2026, 07:45 UTC — carrier notice **with number** |\n| **Tracking number** | **none — not in the order email, not in the shipped email, no attachment** | **SP4471920368PT** (Swiftpost) |\n| Out for delivery | — never sent | 4 Aug 06:30 UTC, SP4471920385PT, window 10:00–13:00 |\n| Delivered | — **never sent** | 4 Aug 11:20 UTC, SP4471920402PT, \"delivered to your mailbox at 11:16\" |\n\nThree things stand out:\n\n1. **Brightloom''s shipped email carries no parcel number.** It says the lamp went \"with Swiftpost\" and offers a \"Track your package\" link, but no reference. Every Swiftpost message for A-38 quotes a full number in `SP############PT` form — so the number exists in that system, it just never reached you for A-42.\n2. **The expected date was 30 Sep 2026 — 41 days ago.** That''s the hard failure, not the missing email: the promised delivery passed six weeks back with no delivery, no delay notice (you did get a \"Your parcel is delayed\" notice on 20 Apr, so this isn''t a channel that never fires), and no return-to-sender message. Since the previous cycle went order → Swiftpost pickup in **2 days**, the absence of any carrier handoff mail in 48 days suggests the parcel was never scanned into the network at all.\n3. **Nothing newer exists.** The last Swiftpost number in the whole mailbox is SP4471920402PT on 4 Aug. The numbering looks sequential, so A-42''s would have slotted in after that — there''s no gap message to find, just silence.\n\nSo the practical position: you have a shipped claim dated 23 Sep, a delivery promise of 30 Sep that has expired, and **no evidence in mail that A-42 was ever physically picked up or moved**.\n\nOne caveat: this is everything searchable in the mailbox, spanning inbox and archive. A delivery notice that got filtered into spam and then deleted would be invisible to me — say the word and I''ll sweep trash and spam for Swiftpost directly.\n\nThe chaser to Brightloom writes itself: ask for **the Swiftpost parcel number for order A-42**, and note that the 30 Sep expected date is 41 days past with no delivery and no scan. Want me to draft it?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:33:15.121Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
