},"updatedAt":1794332085554},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"clearLabel","description":"Remove the label from an email in a specific mailbox.","score":14.51},{"name":"setLabel","description":"Set or change an email''s label in a specific mailbox. The label must be an existing built-in or custom label key — never invent keys.","score":13.87},{"name":"setLabels","description":"Set the same label on several emails in a specific mailbox at once. The label must be an existing key from listLabels. Returns each email''s previou...","score":13.72},{"name":"deleteLabel","description":"Delete a custom label from a specific mailbox. Built-in labels cannot be deleted.","score":12.08},{"name":"createLabel","description":"Create a custom label in a specific mailbox. Returns its key for setLabel and setLabels.","score":11.95}],"loaded":["clearLabel","setLabel","setLabels","deleteLabel","createLabel"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): clearLabel, setLabel, setLabels, deleteLabel, createLabel. They are available on your next turn — call them directly. Some were already loaded."},"toolCallId":"call_bee2355efe8d44f88a4590e5","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"apply label clear label mailbox"}},"updatedAt":1794332085554},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794332085556,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"labels":[{"key":"action_required","builtIn":true},{"key":"work","builtIn":true},{"key":"transactions","builtIn":true},{"key":"updates","builtIn":true},{"key":"newsletter","builtIn":true},{"key":"personal","builtIn":true},{"key":"promotional","builtIn":true},{"key":"social","builtIn":true},{"key":"custom:clients","builtIn":false}]},"toolCallId":"call_eb6a86657d3b44239a96056c","toolName":"listLabels","args":{}},"updatedAt":1794332087673},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794332087676,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"List labels. Nine total: 8 built-in + 1 custom.\n\nPresent clearly. Note the workspace has one mailbox, labels are workspace-level (listLabels returns every label available in the workspace).\n\nMention keys for use with setLabel. Also offer.\n\nKeep concise.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"List labels. Nine total: 8 built-in + 1 custom.\n\nPresent clearly. Note the workspace has one mailbox, labels are workspace-level (listLabels returns every label available in the workspace).\n\nMention keys for use with setLabel. Also offer.\n\nKeep concise."}],"createdAt":1794332096190},{"type":"text","text":"**9 labels** in the workspace — 8 built-in, 1 custom of your own.\n\n**Built-in**\n\n| Key | Looks like it''s for |\n|---|---|\n| `action_required` | mail needing a reply or decision |\n| `work` | studio / client work |\n| `transactions` | bank debits, receipts, orders, deliveries |\n| `updates` | account and service notices |\n| `newsletter` | recurring editorial mail |\n| `personal` | non-work correspondence |\n| `promotional` | shop offers, marketing |\n| `social` | social-network notifications |\n\n**Custom**\n\n- `custom:clients`\n\nUse those keys exactly as written with `setLabel` / `setLabels`, and `clearLabel` to remove one. Built-in keys can''t be deleted; the custom one can.\n\nOne observation from the threads we''ve just been through: `transactions` and `updates` between them cover most of what''s actually sitting in this mailbox — Konkan Bank debits and statements, the Brightloom and Swiftpost order mail, Voltaro receipts. The single custom label `custom:clients` is doing all the client-side work on its own, with no counterpart for vendors or suppliers, which is where the Kestrel Supply and Tavola spending sits.\n\nWant me to file the recent mail — the Konkan debit alerts under `transactions`, the A-42 shipping thread wherever you want it — or create a label like `custom:suppliers` so vendor mail stops competing with `custom:clients`?","createdAt":1794332096190}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**9 labels** in the workspace — 8 built-in, 1 custom of your own.\n\n**Built-in**\n\n| Key | Looks like it''s for |\n|---|---|\n| `action_required` | mail needing a reply or decision |\n| `work` | studio / client work |\n| `transactions` | bank debits, receipts, orders, deliveries |\n| `updates` | account and service notices |\n| `newsletter` | recurring editorial mail |\n| `personal` | non-work correspondence |\n| `promotional` | shop offers, marketing |\n| `social` | social-network notifications |\n\n**Custom**\n\n- `custom:clients`\n\nUse those keys exactly as written with `setLabel` / `setLabels`, and `clearLabel` to remove one. Built-in keys can''t be deleted; the custom one can.\n\nOne observation from the threads we''ve just been through: `transactions` and `updates` between them cover most of what''s actually sitting in this mailbox — Konkan Bank debits and statements, the Brightloom and Swiftpost order mail, Voltaro receipts. The single custom label `custom:clients` is doing all the client-side work on its own, with no counterpart for vendors or suppliers, which is where the Kestrel Supply and Tavola spending sits.\n\nWant me to file the recent mail — the Konkan debit alerts under `transactions`, the A-42 shipping thread wherever you want it — or create a label like `custom:suppliers` so vendor mail stops competing with `custom:clients`?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:34:45.551Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
