m October\" (16 Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (10 Jun 2025) — 2 marketing.\n- Tavola: \"Five new tables in Lisbon this month\" (4 Apr 2025) — 1 marketing; plus \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" (7 Mar 2026) — proof Tavola picks was a newsletter and Ana unsubscribed.\n- Kestrel promos: 2.\n\n**Not newsletters (exclude):** Konkan Bank statements (transactional), Ledgerline invoices (billing), Voltaro bills, Codeyard CI/security notifications, Paperstack sign-in links, verification codes.\n\nTotal newsletter/digest count: 56 (Kestrel) + 5 (Codeyard) + 6 (Paperstack) + 10 (Fernhill studio weekly) = 77 serial. Plus ~9 marketing blasts = 86.\n\nLet me double check Kestrel count 56 — the \"This week at\" search returned count 56, and all entries are Kestrel \"This week at...\" including \"This week at the shop\". Yes.\n\nNote the `newsletter` label exists but I can''t query by label — I should mention that these are unlabeled (I don''t know their labels; I didn''t check). Better: say the built-in `newsletter` label exists and offer to apply it to these.\n\nAlso note: all are read; none unread.\n\nAlso worth noting: Kestrel is the dominant one — 56 of 77, roughly one every 10 days for two years, and it''s a shop Ana also buys from (kestrelsupply@upi debit 19 Jul 2026 INR 3,100). So it''s a vendor newsletter.\n\nAlso: Tavola unsubscribed 7 Mar 2026 — and indeed no Tavola picks after that (last one Apr 2025). Good detail.\n\nAlso Paperstack bi-monthly gap: Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026 — every other month. So \"month\" in subject but bi-monthly delivery.\n\nLet me present with a table, counts, cadence, date range, and offer to label.\n\nDate ranges:\n- Kestrel: 7 Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026 (56)\n- Codeyard digest: 1 Jun 2026 → 7 Sep 2026 (5) — only 5, started June 2026.\n- Paperstack: 2 Nov 2025 → 2 Sep 2026 (6)\n- Fernhill studio weekly: 13 Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026 (10)\n\nMarketing one-offs: Linkroom 4, Northbeam 2, Tavola 1, Kestrel 2 = 9.\n\nTotal 86.\n\nI''ll present clearly.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now compile. Let me categorize.\n\n**Recurring newsletters/digests (true serial publications):**\n\n1. **Kestrel Supply Co.** — \"This week at Kestrel: …\" weekly-ish. Count: the \"This week at\" search returned 56. Let me count precisely from the \"This week at\" result (count 56). That includes \"This week at the shop\" (26 Sep 2026) and all \"This week at Kestrel: ...\" — 56 total. Range: 7 Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026. Cadence: roughly every 10 days (not strictly weekly). Plus 2 promotional one-offs from Kestrel: \"15% off this weekend only\" (14 Aug 2026) and \"Spring sale starts now\" (20 Mar 2026) — those are promotional, not newsletter.\n\n2. **Codeyard** — \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" — count from digest search: 7 (7 Sep, 24 Aug, 27 Jul, 29 Jun, 1 Jun 2026... let me count: Sep 07, Aug 24, Jul 27, Jun 29, Jun 01 = 5 in 2026). Hmm the digest search returned 11 total: 5 Codeyard digests + 6 Paperstack months. Let me recount Codeyard digests: Sep 07 2026, Aug 24 2026, Jul 27 2026, Jun 29 2026, Jun 01 2026 = 5. Yes 5.\n\n3. **Paperstack** — \"Your Paperstack month: <Month> <Year>\" — monthly. From digest search: Sep 2026, Jul 2026, May 2026, Mar 2026, Jan 2026, Nov 2025 = 6. Note: odd months only — Feb, Apr, Jun, Aug, Oct, Dec missing. Interesting: it''s bi-monthly in practice, or gaps. Actually Sep, Jul, May, Mar, Jan, Nov = every other month. So it''s effectively bi-monthly despite saying \"month\".\n\n4. **Priya Nair — \"[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly, <date>\"** — internal team digest, weekly. Count from \"weekly\" search: 14 Sep 2026, 13 Jul 2026, 11 May 2026, 9 Feb 2026, 10 Nov 2025, 15 Sep 2025, 14 Jul 2025, 12 May 2025, 10 Mar 2025, 13 Jan 2025 = 10. That''s internal, not marketing — worth distinguishing.\n\n**Product marketing / one-off announcements (newsletter-ish but not serial):**\n- Linkroom: \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\" (8 Sep 2026), \"Breakout rooms are here\" (21 Apr 2026), \"Linkroom rooms now remember your layout\" (23 Sep 2025), \"New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages\" (18 Feb 2025) — 4 product-announcement blasts.\n- Northbeam Air: \"Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt, new route from October\" (16 Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (10 Jun 2025) — 2 marketing.\n- Tavola: \"Five new tables in Lisbon this month\" (4 Apr 2025) — 1 marketing; plus \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" (7 Mar 2026) — proof Tavola picks was a newsletter and Ana unsubscribed.\n- Kestrel promos: 2.\n\n**Not newsletters (exclude):** Konkan Bank statements (transactional), Ledgerline invoices (billing), Voltaro bills, Codeyard CI/security notifications, Paperstack sign-in links, verification codes.\n\nTotal newsletter/digest count: 56 (Kestrel) + 5 (Codeyard) + 6 (Paperstack) + 10 (Fernhill studio weekly) = 77 serial. Plus ~9 marketing blasts = 86.\n\nLet me double check Kestrel count 56 — the \"This week at\" search returned count 56, and all entries are Kestrel \"This week at...\" including \"This week at the shop\". Yes.\n\nNote the `newsletter` label exists but I can''t query by label — I should mention that these are unlabeled (I don''t know their labels; I didn''t check). Better: say the built-in `newsletter` label exists and offer to apply it to these.\n\nAlso note: all are read; none unread.\n\nAlso worth noting: Kestrel is the dominant one — 56 of 77, roughly one every 10 days for two years, and it''s a shop Ana also buys from (kestrelsupply@upi debit 19 Jul 2026 INR 3,100). So it''s a vendor newsletter.\n\nAlso: Tavola unsubscribed 7 Mar 2026 — and indeed no Tavola picks after that (last one Apr 2025). Good detail.\n\nAlso Paperstack bi-monthly gap: Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026 — every other month. So \"month\" in subject but bi-monthly delivery.\n\nLet me present with a table, counts, cadence, date range, and offer to label.\n\nDate ranges:\n- Kestrel: 7 Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026 (56)\n- Codeyard digest: 1 Jun 2026 → 7 Sep 2026 (5) — only 5, started June 2026.\n- Paperstack: 2 Nov 2025 → 2 Sep 2026 (6)\n- Fernhill studio weekly: 13 Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026 (10)\n\nMarketing one-offs: Linkroom 4, Northbeam 2, Tavola 1, Kestrel 2 = 9.\n\nTotal 86.\n\nI''ll present clearly."}],"createdAt":1794332235194},{"type":"text","text":"**86 emails** in `ana@demo.trymetis.email` read as newsletters or digests — **77 of them from four recurring serials**, the rest one-off marketing blasts. All are already read; none are in the unread pile.\n\n**The recurring serials**\n\n| Sender | Subject pattern | Count | Cadence | Span |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kestrel Supply Co.** | \"This week at Kestrel: …\" | **56** | ~every 10 days | 7 Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026 |\n| **Priya Nair** (internal) | \"[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly, \\<date\\>\" | **10** | weekly-ish | 13 Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026 |\n| **Paperstack** | \"Your Paperstack month: \\<Month Year\\>\" | **6** | every *other* month | 2 Nov 2025 → 2 Sep 2026 |\n| **Codeyard** | \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" | **5** | weekly | 1 Jun 2026 → 7 Sep 2026 |\n\n**One-off marketing / product announcements** (9)\n\n- **Linkroom** — 4: *Linkroom for teams: shared recordings* (8 Sep 2026), *Breakout rooms are here* (21 Apr 2026), *Linkroom rooms now remember your layout* (23 Sep 2025), *New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages* (18 Feb 2025)\n- **Northbeam Air** — 2: *Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt, new route from October* (16 Jun 2026), *Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79* (10 Jun 2025)\n- **Kestrel Supply Co.** — 2 promos outside the weekly: *15% off this weekend only* (14 Aug 2026), *Spring sale starts now* (20 Mar 2026)\n- **Tavola** — 1: *Five new tables in Lisbon this month* (4 Apr 2025)\n\n**Four things worth knowing**\n\n1. **Kestrel is 65% of the whole pile** — 56 emails over 23 months, and it''s a shop you actually buy from (the INR 3,100 UPI debit to `kestrelsupply@upi` on 19 Jul 2026). It''s a vendor newsletter, not a