|\n| 7 | **S3 bucket** | `1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60` | whole drive |\n\nTwo things stand out:\n\n- **Three separate FTP servers** and **two S3 buckets** — a fairly scattered file estate for one person. If some of these are hosts you no longer use, this is the moment to notice.\n- **Six of the seven expose the entire drive** to this workspace. Only #3 (`766b212a…`) is scoped to specific folders. So anything generated or stored in the other six is fully visible to workspace tools — worth confirming that''s what you intended, particularly for the S3 buckets, which often hold backups.\n\nIf you want names instead of UUIDs, I can list the top level of each drive — seven calls, and you''ll get a folder tree that makes them self-identifying. I can then pin the ones you use regularly so you stop hunting for ids. Say the word and I''ll browse all seven at once.","createdAt":1794332253435}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**7 drives** are connected, all under `ana@demo.trymetis.email`. The listing gives me provider and scope but no display names — you''ll recognise them by what''s inside, so I''ve listed the ids you''d use.\n\n| # | Provider | driveId | Scope |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **SFTP** | `36600459-5ed5-55e6-8cb3-f158ce3b8910` | whole drive |\n| 2 | **FTP** | `d4dacf11-803f-51a6-a691-71b4bef60633` | whole drive |\n| 3 | **FTP** | `766b212a-2055-54c0-92da-efe26ae6541b` | **folders only** |\n| 4 | **FTP** | `42ffd478-fdb0-5b94-a927-24af30e1d0e8` | whole drive |\n| 5 | **WebDAV** | `cc3fbded-3385-56f1-9b18-d589faa3437a` | whole drive |\n| 6 | **S3 bucket** | `b4199497-5df2-5d9e-bd43-347298cdaad1` | whole drive |\n| 7 | **S3 bucket** | `1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60` | whole drive |\n\nTwo things stand out:\n\n- **Three separate FTP servers** and **two S3 buckets** — a fairly scattered file estate for one person. If some of these are hosts you no longer use, this is the moment to