md 574. Identical across all six.\n  - One discrepancy: on WebDAV (cc3fbded) Meeting notes 2026-10-05.md has mimeType \"text/plain\" whereas on SFTP (36600459) it''s \"text/markdown\". And FTP drives have mimeType null. S3 has null. So mime types differ per provider — cosmetic/metadata difference, not content.\n- Finance/: only \"2025\" folder on all — need to go deeper to know files. Not yet compared.\n- Clients/: same three folders: Aozora Ceramics, Kaltwasser GmbH, Saffron & Sage. Order differs (alphabetical vs insertion). Count 3 everywhere.\n  - Note drive 3 (scoped FTP) shows only Clients/ with the same 3 subfolders.\n\nSo: 6 drives look like complete mirrors of one another; the 7th (folder-scoped FTP) exposes only Clients/ — a subset, not a mirror.\n\nDifferences found so far:\n1. Drive 3 (766b212a, FTP, folder-scoped): root has ONLY Clients/ — no Team, Finance, welcome.txt. It''s a scoped view, not a separate store. Whether it''s the same underlying store as another FTP drive is unverifiable from here, but content under Clients matches.\n2. Drives 6 and 7 (both S3) have an extra `edge/` folder at root — test-fixture content (big, bulk-2500, case, deep, docs, empty-folder, folder-marker, images, mislabeled, preview, special, unicode, empty.txt, no-content-type.bin, one-byte) — identical in both buckets (same 15 entries, same sizes).\n3. mimeType differs across providers (md as text/markdown on SFTP vs text/plain on WebDAV vs null on FTP/S3).\n4. Timestamps: SFTP (36600459) and WebDAV (cc3fbded) stamp every entry 2026-11-10T17:28:49Z; S3 (both) stamp at 17:28:25.755–.846Z; FTP drives report null modifiedAt everywhere. So all seven were touched within the last ~9 minutes of this turn clock — meaning these are freshly synced/mounted, and the timestamps can''t be used as real modification history.\n\nI should verify deeper to be confident about Finance/ and Clients/ subfolder contents. The remaining unknown: contents of Clients/<client>/ and Finance/2025/ and Tea