stInvites","args":{}},"updatedAt":1794332352591},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794332352592,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Only one member: Ana Silva, owner. No pending invites.\n\nI should answer clearly and note the implication: all the mailboxes/drives are hers; no colleagues have access. The people appearing in mail (Raj Mehta, Priya Nair, Sam Okafor, Tomás Ortega, Kenji Watanabe, Layla Haddad, Mira Costa, Cy Reyes, Lena Hoffmann) are external correspondents, not workspace members — worth clarifying since the user might think of them as colleagues. Let me distinguish.\n\nI should be careful: I know from mail who the correspondents are. They''re not members (only 1 member returned). People on @demo.trymetis.email domain appear as senders (Raj Mehta, Priya Nair, Sam Okafor, Tomás Ortega, Mira Costa) — same domain as Ana, which might suggest they''re colleagues, but they are not workspace members. That''s worth flagging as an observation but without overclaiming — the workspace sees only one member, so they don''t have access here.\n\nFormat: short table, then note.\n\nAlso mention: since only Ana is a member, the earlier \"colleague availability\" tools would only ever return her events.\n\nI''ll mention listInvites returned none — so no one is mid-way into the workspace.\n\nDon''t overdo it. Keep it tight but useful.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Only one member: Ana Silva, owner. No pending invites.\n\nI should answer clearly and note the implication: all the mailboxes/drives are hers; no colleagues have access. The people appearing in mail (Raj Mehta, Priya Nair, Sam Okafor, Tomás Ortega, Kenji Watanabe, Layla Haddad, Mira Costa, Cy Reyes, Lena Hoffmann) are external correspondents, not workspace members — worth clarifying since the user might think of them as colleagues. Let me distinguish.\n\nI should be careful: I know from mail who the correspondents are. They''re not members (only 1 member returned). People on @demo.trymetis.email domain appear as senders (Raj Mehta, Priya Nair, Sam Okafor, Tomás Ortega, Mira Costa) — same domain as Ana, which might suggest they''re colleagues, but they are not workspace members. That''s worth flagging as an observation but without overclaiming — the workspace sees only one member, so they don''t have access here.\n\nFormat: short table, then note.\n\nAlso mention: since only Ana is a member, the earlier \"colleague availability\" tools would only ever return her events.\n\nI''ll mention listInvites returned none — so no one is mid-way into the workspace.\n\nDon''t overdo it. Keep it tight but useful."}],"createdAt":1794332361514},{"type":"text","text":"**One member.** This workspace has a single person in it.\n\n| Name | Email | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ana Silva | `ana@demo.trymetis.email` | owner |\n\nNo pending invitations either — nothing in flight. So this is effectively a personal workspace: every mailbox, calendar and drive the tools can reach belongs to you, and there''s nobody else''s data in scope.\n\nOne thing worth clearing up, because it''s easy to misread: a number of people who write to you share your `@demo.trymetis.email` domain — **Raj Mehta**, **Priya Nair**, **Sam Okafor**, **Tomás Ortega**, **Mira Costa** — along with outside contacts like **Kenji Watanabe** (Aozora Ceramics), **Layla Haddad** (Saffron & Sage), **Lena Hoffmann** (Kaltwasser) and **Cy Reyes**. None of them is a workspace member; they''re correspondents who appear in your mail. They have no access to this workspace, and the member tools won''t see their files or calendars.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n- Any question about \"what''s on the team''s calendars\" resolves to just your own — there''s no colleague to compare against.\n- Everyone you delegate or share with has to be invited first. Say the word and I can tell you what the invitation flow looks like, or leave it as is.","createdAt":1794332361514}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**One member.** This workspace has a single person in it.\n\n| Name | Email | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ana Silva | `ana@demo.trymetis.email` | owner |\n\nNo pending invitations either — nothing in flight. So this is effectively a personal workspace: every mailbox, calendar and drive the tools can reach belongs to you, and there''s nobody else''s data in scope.\n\nOne thing worth clearing up, because it''s easy to misread: a number of people who write to you share your `@demo.trymetis.email` domain — **Raj Mehta**, **Priya Nair**, **Sam Okafor**, **Tomás Ortega**, **Mira Costa** — along with outside contacts like **Kenji Watanabe** (Aozora Ceramics), **Layla Haddad** (Saffron & Sage), **Lena Hoffmann** (Kaltwasser) and **Cy Reyes**. None of them is a workspace member; they''re correspondents who appear in your mail. They have no access to this workspace, and the member tools won''t see their files or calendars.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n- Any question about \"what''s on the team''s calendars\" resolves to just your own — there''s no colleague to compare against.\n- Everyone you delegate or share with has to be invited first. Say the word and I can tell you what the invitation flow looks like, or leave it as is."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:39:07.161Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
