INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('1bdc3440-31f1-49e8-99aa-499de9973b71','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user wants a prioritized to-do list for \"this week\" based on everything above. Turn sent 2026-11-10T17:39:21Z, UTC. So \"this week\" = Mon 9 Nov 2026 – Sun 15 Nov 2026 (10 Nov 2026 is a Tuesday? Let me check: 10 Nov 2026 — Jan 1 2026 is a Thursday. Let me compute day of week for Nov 10, 2026.\n\n2026-11-10: Use known anchor: 2026-01-01 is Thursday. Day-of-year for Nov 10: Jan 31, Feb 28 (2026 not leap), Mar 31, Apr 30, May 31, Jun 30, Jul 31, Aug 31, Sep 30, Oct 31 = 304; +10 = 314. Day 1 = Thursday. (314-1) mod 7 = 313 mod 7 = 313 - 308 = 5. Thursday +5 = Tuesday. So 10 Nov 2026 is a Tuesday. Week Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026.\n\nNow, \"based on everything above\" — above covers: mailboxes (one mailbox, ana@demo.trymetis.email), unread count (278 fixtures, 0 real), newsletters (86), drives (7, six mirrors + scoped subset + S3 edge/), workspace members (1).\n\nBut a to-do list for this week should be grounded in actual upcoming commitments. From the earlier inbox listing I saw calendar-ish items:\n- Northbeam Air: \"Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9\" (3 Sep 2026) — that''s a flight on 9 Nov 2026, which is Monday — possibly already departed, or today-ish. Actually confirmed booking for Nov 9 — the flight date. That''s yesterday/today.\n- Aozora packaging call: \"Invitation: Aozora packaging call @ Thu Oct 15, 2026 09:00 JST\" — past.\n- Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 — past.\n- Aozora logo review (internal) @ Thu Oct 1, 2026 — past.\n- Aozora logo review @ Wed Sep 30, 2026 — past.\n- Linkroom Pro plan renews on October 3 — past.\n- Ledgerline trial ended — past.\n- Voltaro bill — Sep.\n- Swiggy/etc.\n\nHmm — the inbox''s most recent email is 26 Sep 2026, and today is 10 Nov 2026. So there''s a ~6-week gap: nothing in the inbox after 26 Sep. The most recent mail is from 26 Sep. That''s notable.\n\nTo build a credible to-do list for THIS week, I should check the calendar for the current week (9–15 Nov 2026). That''s the right tool: listEvents (need to search for it). Also I could check for recent mail that''s unread/needing action — but we know there''s none.\n\nAlso, there''s a notable item: the Northbeam booking Lisbon→Tokyo on 9 Nov 2026, and Kenji Watanabe''s Aozora branding work with a Japan contact. And the inbox has a gap.\n\nGiven the user said \"based on everything above\", they may want the list to be built from the findings in this conversation. But a good prioritized to-do list for the week should include real calendar commitments. I think I should check the calendar for this week to ground it. Let me search for the calendar event listing tool and list calendars, then list events for 9–15 Nov 2026.\n\nThat''s a reasonable amount of work: search_tools(\"list calendar events\"), listCalendars, then listEvents.\n\nLet me do that. I''ll search for both \"list calendar events in a time window\" and \"open one event\".\n\nActually listCalendars is always loaded. Let me call listCalendars and search_tools in parallel.\n\nAlso the mail side: I should check whether there''s unread/actionable mail that was missed. The inbox is all read and the newest is 26 Sep 2026 — six weeks stale. Maybe I should check other folders (archive?) — no, \"inbox right now\" was the question earlier. But for a to-do list, recent mail matters. There might be newer mail in the mailbox that isn''t in the inbox (e.g., trash/spam). Hmm, searchMail searches all. Let me do a broad recent check: searchMail for \"Aozora\" and maybe list the most recent across the mailbox. Actually aggregateInbox gives most recent inbox emails per mailbox — I already have that from turn 1? No, I never called aggregateInbox. I listed the inbox beginning, which is sorted by date descending and the newest was 26 Sep 2026.\n\nTo be safe for \"this week\", I''ll check the calendar (the main source of dated commitments) and maybe check sent/drafts for pending replies. Let me keep it focused: calendar for this week is the key addition.\n\nLet me search tools for calendar events listing and open event.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user wants a prioritized to-do list for \"this week\" based on everything above. Turn sent 2026-11-10T17:39:21Z, UTC. So \"this week\" = Mon 9 Nov 2026 – Sun 15 Nov 2026 (10 Nov 2026 is a Tuesday? Let me check: 10 Nov 2026 — Jan 1 2026 is a Thursday. Let me compute day of week for Nov 10, 2026.\n\n2026-11-10: Use known anchor: 2026-01-01 is Thursday. Day-of-year for Nov 10: Jan 31, Feb 28 (2026 not leap), Mar 31, Apr 30, May 31, Jun 30, Jul 31, Aug 31, Sep 30, Oct 31 = 304; +10 = 314. Day 1 = Thursday. (314-1) mod 7 = 313 mod 7 = 313 - 308 = 5. Thursday +5 = Tuesday. So 10 Nov 2026 is a Tuesday. Week Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026.\n\nNow, \"based on everything above\" — above covers: mailboxes (one mailbox, ana@demo.trymetis.email), unread count (278 fixtures, 0 real), newsletters (86), drives (7, six mirrors + scoped subset + S3 edge/), workspace members (1).\n\nBut a to-do list for this week should be grounded in actual upcoming commitments. From the earlier inbox listing I saw calendar-ish items:\n- Northbeam Air: \"Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9\" (3 Sep 2026) — that''s a flight on 9 Nov 2026, which is Monday — possibly already departed, or today-ish. Actually confirmed booking for Nov 9 — the flight date. That''s yesterday/today.\n- Aozora packaging call: \"Invitation: Aozora packaging call @ Thu Oct 15, 2026 09:00 JST\" — past.\n- Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 — past.\n- Aozora logo review (internal) @ Thu Oct 1, 2026 — past.\n- Aozora logo review @ Wed Sep 30, 2026 — past.\n- Linkroom Pro plan renews on October 3 — past.\n- Ledgerline trial ended — past.\n- Voltaro bill — Sep.\n- Swiggy/etc.\n\nHmm — the inbox''s