er** — Edge cases calendar, 09:00–09:15 daily — fixture, overlaps the standup. Should be flagged as fixture.\n- **Ten year all-day event** — Edge cases, 2026-01-01 → 2036-01-01, so it covers this whole week — fixture, spans a decade. It''s why every week looks \"busy\".\n- **Bulk 1–299 events** — Bulk calendar, fixture noise: 8 per day at 4-hour intervals (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 etc.), 45-min each. In this week''s window: 92 total events, minus the 2 real recurring ones... let me count how many are Bulk in the 9–15 Nov window. The list had 92 entries. Non-Bulk: Ten year all-day (1, edge), Daily forever ×7 (edge: 9,10,11,12,13,14,15), Daily standup ×5 (9,10,11,12,13), Weekly 1:1 ×1 (10), Tokyo trip (1, personal all-day). That''s 1+7+5+1+1 = 15. So Bulk = 92 - 15 = 77. Hmm, but \"Ten year all-day\" spans and may be returned once. Let me just say ~77 bulk fixtures in the week.\n\nActually let me recount precisely: 92 events returned. Bulk events: I can count the ones titled \"Bulk N ...\". Listing day by day from the output:\nNov 9: bulk-288, bulk-120, bulk-148, bulk-176, bulk-8, bulk-204, bulk-36, bulk-232, bulk-64, bulk-260, bulk-92 = 11\nNov 10: bulk-289, bulk-121, bulk-149, bulk-177, bulk-9, bulk-205, bulk-37, bulk-233, bulk-65, bulk-261, bulk-93 = 11\nNov 11: bulk-290, bulk-122, bulk-150, bulk-178, bulk-10, bulk-206, bulk-38, bulk-234, bulk-66, bulk-262, bulk-94 = 11\nNov 12: bulk-291, bulk-123, bulk-151, bulk-179, bulk-11, bulk-207, bulk-39, bulk-235, bulk-67, bulk-263, bulk-95 = 11\nNov 13: bulk-264, bulk-96, bulk-292, bulk-124, bulk-152, bulk-180, bulk-12, bulk-208, bulk-40, bulk-236, bulk-68 = 11\nNov 14: bulk-265, bulk-97, bulk-293, bulk-125, bulk-153, bulk-181, bulk-13, bulk-209, bulk-41, bulk-237, bulk-69 = 11\nNov 15: bulk-266, bulk-98, bulk-294, bulk-126, bulk-154, bulk-182, bulk-14, bulk-210, bulk-42, bulk-238, bulk-70 = 11\nTotal bulk = 77. Yes.\n\nNon-bulk = 92 - 77 = 15: Ten year all-day (1), Tokyo trip (1), Daily forever ×7 (9,10,11,12,13,14,15 — I count 7 occurrences), Daily standup ×5 (9–13), Weekly 1:1 (10). 1+1+7+5+1 = 15. ✓\n\nSo of 92 events in the week, 13 are fixtures (77 Bulk + 7 Daily forever + 1 Ten-year = 85 fixtures) and 4 distinct real series/items: Tokyo trip, Daily standup (5 occurrences), Weekly 1:1.\n\nReal distinct: Tokyo trip (all week), Daily standup ×5, Weekly 1:1 ×1. Fixtures: 85.\n\nAlso the 1:1 Ana/Raj has attendee ana@demo.trymetis.email — only herself listed as attendee. Location linkroom.app/r/ana-raj.\n\nNow, the drafts folder — 6 drafts, all from Ana Silva herself, dated 12–20 Sep 2026, subjects:\n1. \"Studio tidy-up on Friday\" (20 Sep)\n2. \"Terms for November 26\" (19 Sep)\n3. \"رد: تصميم القائمة الجديدة / New menu design\" (18 Sep) — Arabic, Saffron & Sage\n4. \"Fwd: Budget 2026 so far\" (17 Sep)\n5. \"Wartung der Website\" (16 Sep) — German, Kaltwasser\n6. \"Packaging samples\" (12 Sep)\n\nSix unsent drafts, oldest 12 Sep, newest 20 Sep 2026 — all ~7 weeks stale. These are the closest thing to \"real to-dos\" in the mail.\n\nNote \"Terms for November 26\" — could relate to a November 26 deadline. And Tavola \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\".\n\nRead-later has 1 item: id WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwN10 = \"Brightloom — Your order A-42 has shipped\" (23 Sep 2026, from the first inbox page). Yes, that id matches the Brightloom order shipped email. So the single read-later item is a shipping notice for order A-42.\n\nSnoozed: none.\n\nMail: newest mail is 26 Sep 2026 — six weeks before now. So no new mail.\n\nAlso relevant from earlier context:\n- Northbeam booking: \"Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9\" (starred, 3 Sep 2026) — matches the Tokyo trip all-day event 9–15 Nov. So the trip is happening NOW: she flew Lisbon→Tokyo on 9 Nov. That''s a strong tied-together finding.\n- Kenji Watanabe (Aozora) sent \"Invitation: Aozora packaging call @ Thu Oct 15, 2026 09:00 JST\" — in the past. And \"新ブランド案のご確認について\" (about confirming the new brand proposal) 10 Sep — unanswered? It was read. Hmm, I shouldn''t overclaim about replies I haven''t checked. But drafts include nothing for Kenji.\n- Aozora-related: \"Rebrand kickoff\", \"Aozora review agenda\", proposal signed, logo reviews. The drive has Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Proposal - signed.pdf and a Rebrand/ folder.\n- Saffron & Sage: Priya Nair \"Arabic proofs\" (18 Sep), Layla Haddad \"Menu print run\" (20 Aug), Arabic menu design thread.\n- Kaltwasser GmbH: Lena Hoffmann \"Wartung ab Oktober\" (31 Aug), \"AW: Rechnung FS-2026-031\" (21 Jul).\n- Ledgerline trial ended; Voltaro bill paid.\n- Linkroom Pro plan renews October 3 (past).\n- Finance/2025/ in the drive has Budget 2025.xlsx, expenses.tsv, invoices.csv — and there''s a \"Fwd: Budget 2026 so far\" draft. Note: the drive only has Finance/2025 — no 2026 folder. Worth flagging.\n\nSo the to-do list should combine:\nA. Time-critical this week: the Tokyo trip (9–15 Nov) — she''s in Japan; the Aozora packaging call was 15 Oct (past); the Weekly 1:1 Ana/Raj on Tue 10 Nov 10:00 UTC — question: Tokyo is UTC+9, so 10:00 UTC = 19:00 JST. That''s a real scheduling wrinkle worth flagging. Standup 09:00 UTC = 18:00 JST. That''s an important, actionable insight: her recurring work meetings now land in the evening JST while she''s in Tokyo.\nB. Six stale drafts to resolve (send or delete): these are actual unfinished work. Prioritize by client/date.\nC. The 1 read-later item (Brightloom A-42 shipped) — trivial, clear it.\nD. Workspace hygiene items from earlier in the conversation: 278 unread fixtures (mark read/archive), 86 newsletters (label), Codeyard digest anomalies (not actionable), the 7 drives (settle whether they''re independent copies), workspace has 1 member (invite colleagues if needed).\nE. Calendar hygiene: 85 fixture events polluting the week (Bulk calendar 77 + Daily forever 7 + Ten-year 1). The Daily forever at 09:00 collides exactly with the real Daily standup 09:00–09:15. Worth flagging as a genuine problem: any automation on \"next meeting\" would pick the fixture.\n\nAlso: Kenji Watanabe''s unanswered Japanese email about confirming the new brand proposal — I should be careful. I don''t know if she replied (I only looked at inbox). I could check sent folder for replies to Kenji. That would strengthen the to-do. But is it worth another tool call? The user asked for a prioritized to-do list; verifying whether Kenji''s 10 Sep email got a reply is important because that''s a client deliverable. Also Priya''s \"Arabic proofs\" 18 Sep and Layla''s \"Menu print run\". Hmm.\n\nActually, notifications: Kenji sent \"Automatic reply: Re: Aozora rebrand: logo shortlist\" on 4 Sep — auto-reply, meaning he was away. And 10 Sep he asked about confirming the new brand proposal (新ブランド案のご確認について). Also an Aozora packaging call invitation for 15 Oct.\n\nI think checking the sent folder would be valuable to determine which client threads are awaiting her reply. Let me do that — one call, sent folder, limit 50. That directly affects prioritization. Let me also check the archive/starred? The starred items: Mira Costa \"Re: Venue for the Aozora launch\" (starred), Northbeam booking (starred), Kenji \"Aozora rebrand: brief and timeline\" (starred), Raj \"Aozora proposal signed\" (starred), Lena \"AW: Rechnung FS-2026-031\" (starred), Layla \"New menu design\" (starred), Tomás \"[Fernhill Team] Photos from the offsite\" (starred), Priya \"Introducing Layla Haddad\" (starred).\n\nLet me fetch the sent folder to see what she last replied to. That''s one more call. I''ll do it, then write the list.\n\nActually — I have enough to build a strong list. But \"prioritized to-do list for this week\" deserves accuracy about open loops. The sent folder is the key to knowing which client threads are unanswered. Let me check it. One call, limit 50.\n\nLet me do that.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me analyze this week (Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026).\n\nReal (non-fixture) events this