on & Sage. If you answered these by phone or in person, ignore me — I can only see that nothing went out.\n\n**4. Confirm the Aozora launch venue.** You sent *Venue for the Aozora launch* (8 Sep) and *Harbour Hall hold* (9 Sep), and Mira Costa''s reply is one of your eight starred messages. The hold has been sitting nearly nine weeks with no follow-up in the mailbox.\n\n## P2 — This week if time allows\n\n**5. Check how you''re getting home.** The only travel mail is *Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9* (Northbeam, starred). There''s no return leg anywhere in the mailbox, and the `Tokyo trip` calendar entry ends 15 Nov. Worth confirming you have a flight back.\n\n**6. Clear the one read-later item** — the Brightloom *order A-42 has shipped* notice from 23 Sep. One item, thirty seconds.\n\n**7. File your 2026 finance.** The drives carry `Finance/2025/` only (`Budget 2025.xlsx`, `expenses.tsv`, `invoices.csv`) — but your own draft is titled *Fwd: Budget 2026 so far*. Ten months of 2026 has nowhere to live.\n\n## P3 — Fifteen minutes of cleanup\n\n**8. Kill the 278 unread fixtures** — mark read or archive. Any unread-based view or rule is currently 100% noise.\n\n**9. Deal with 85 calendar fixtures masking the week** — 77 `Bulk N …` events plus `Daily forever` and a `Ten year all-day event` running 2026→2036. **`Daily forever` sits at exactly 09:00 UTC, the same slot as your real standup**, so anything asking \"what''s next\" will pick the fake one.\n\n**10. Label the 86 newsletters**, or take Kestrel up on the unsubscribe offer — 56 of those 86 are theirs.\n\n**11. Settle the drive question.** Six of your seven drives hold byte-identical copies of the same tree; one sees only `Clients/`. If they''re six independent copies rather than one store mounted six ways, your `Budget 2025.xlsx` edits won''t propagate and you''ll have no way to tell which copy is current.\n\n---\n\n**Why this order:** Tokyo is the only thing with a clock on it this week, the 