INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('aee402fd-e515-40e7-9c8f-15e6a17eb220','3f132823-cb61-42f9-9d97-ac2645138d80','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user wants a short status update they could paste into chat. So a compact, paste-ready message. Should be plain, scannable, chat-appropriate. Probably a short block of text with a few bullets. Not markdown-heavy tables — chat paste. Maybe keep light markdown since chat may render it.\n\nKeep it short. Include: where she stands (in Tokyo, week of 9–15 Nov), the few real commitments, the open loops. Drop the workspace-hygiene items (not appropriate for a team chat? maybe one line). Should be brief — \"short status update.\"\n\nLet me draft:\n\nSomething like:\n\n**Status — week of 9–15 Nov**\n\nIn Tokyo until the 15th. Calendar''s basically clear: daily standup (18:00 JST this week) and next Tuesday''s 1:1. Back Monday 16th.\n\nOpen:\n- Six drafts written mid-September, still unsent — clearing them this week. \"Terms for November 26\" first.\n- Aozora: owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal confirmation (his 10 Sep note). Chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n- Saffron & Sage: Arabic proofs from Priya (18 Sep) still unanswered.\n- Need to confirm my return flight.\n\nAlso flag: nothing in or out of the inbox since late September.\n\nHmm — should I mention the mail dormancy? It''s a real status fact. Could phrase: \"Inbox has been quiet since late Sept — catching up on what''s outstanding.\"\n\nShould I include the workspace hygiene? Probably one short line: \"Also cleaning up a pile of test noise in mail/calendar.\" That''s honest and useful.\n\nKeep it to ~120-150 words. Chat paste. Let me make it tight and copy-pasteable with minimal markup.\n\nI''ll present it as a quoted block so it''s easy to copy. Maybe give it directly. Use a light touch.\n\nLet me not include the internal analysis caveat language (like \"no reply in the mailbox\") — but accuracy matters: don''t overclaim. Say \"still owing Kenji a reply\" as a commitment, which is her own framing.\n\nDraft final:\n\n**Week of 9–15 Nov**\n- In Tokyo through the 15th; back at my desk Monday 16th.\n- Calendar''s clear apart from the daily standup (18:00 JST this week). Nothing else scheduled.\n- Mail''s been quiet since late September — using this week to close out what''s open:\n  • Six drafts I wrote mid-Sept and never sent. Sending this week, starting with the Nov 26 terms.\n  • Aozora — owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal, and I need to chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n  • Saffron & Sage — Arabic proofs from Priya still need my sign-off.\n  • Confirming my return flight.\n- One housekeeping item: clearing out a chunk of test noise in my mail and calendar.\n\nThat''s good. Maybe trim slightly. Prefix with one line \"Quick status:\" ? I''ll just give the block, and a one-line note that it''s ready to paste and that I dropped the internal-only items.\n\nShould I note what I dropped? Briefly — yes, one line: I left out the internal clean-up detail (drives, fixtures) except one line. Actually I included one line about test noise. Fine.\n\nKeep the framing minimal.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user wants a short status update they could paste into chat. So a compact, paste-ready message. Should be plain, scannable, chat-appropriate. Probably a short block of text with a few bullets. Not markdown-heavy tables — chat paste. Maybe keep light markdown since chat may render it.\n\nKeep it short. Include: where she stands (in Tokyo, week of 9–15 Nov), the few real commitments, the open loops. Drop the workspace-hygiene items (not appropriate for a team chat? maybe one line). Should be brief — \"short status update.\"\n\nLet me draft:\n\nSomething like:\n\n**Status — week of 9–15 Nov**\n\nIn Tokyo until the 15th. Calendar''s basically clear: daily standup (18:00 JST this week) and next Tuesday''s 1:1. Back Monday 16th.\n\nOpen:\n- Six drafts written mid-September, still unsent — clearing them this week. \"Terms for November 26\" first.\n- Aozora: owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal confirmation (his 10 Sep note). Chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n- Saffron & Sage: Arabic proofs from Priya (18 Sep) still unanswered.\n- Need to confirm my return flight.\n\nAlso flag: nothing in or out of the inbox since late September.\n\nHmm — should I mention the mail dormancy? It''s a real status fact. Could phrase: \"Inbox has been quiet since late Sept — catching up on what''s outstanding.\"\n\nShould I include the workspace hygiene? Probably one short line: \"Also cleaning up a pile of test noise in mail/calendar.\" That''s honest and useful.\n\nKeep it to ~120-150 words. Chat paste. Let me make it tight and copy-pasteable with minimal markup.\n\nI''ll present it as a quoted block so it''s easy to copy. Maybe give it directly. Use a light touch.\n\nLet me not include the internal analysis caveat language (like \"no reply in the mailbox\") — but accuracy matters: don''t overclaim. Say \"still owing Kenji a reply\" as a commitment, which is her own framing.\n\nDraft final:\n\n**Week of 9–15 Nov**\n- In Tokyo through the 15th; back at my desk Monday 16th.\n- Calendar''s clear apart from the daily standup (18:00 JST this week). Nothing else scheduled.\n- Mail''s been quiet since late September — using this week to close out what''s open:\n  • Six drafts I wrote mid-Sept and never sent. Sending this week, starting with the Nov 26 terms.\n  • Aozora — owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal, and I need to chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n  • Saffron & Sage — Arabic proofs from Priya still need my sign-off.\n  • Confirming my return flight.\n- One housekeeping item: clearing out a chunk of test noise in my mail and calendar.\n\nThat''s good. Maybe trim slightly. Prefix with one line \"Quick status:\" ? I''ll just give the block, and a one-line note that it''s ready to paste and that I dropped the internal-only items.\n\nShould I note what I dropped? Briefly — yes, one line: I left out the internal clean-up detail (drives, fixtures) except one line. Actually I included one line about test noise. Fine.\n\nKeep the framing minimal."}],"createdAt":1794332485173},{"type":"text","text":"Here''s a paste-ready version — trimmed to the things a colleague needs to know, with the workspace-hygiene detail collapsed to one line:\n\n---\n\n**Week of 9–15 Nov**\n\n- In Tokyo through the 15th, back at my desk Monday the 16th.\n- Calendar is clear apart from the daily standup (18:00 JST this week). Nothing else on.\n- Mail''s been quiet since late September, so I''m using the week to close out what''s open:\n  - Six drafts I wrote mid-September and never sent. Going out this week, starting with the **Nov 26 terms**.\n  - **Aozora** — I owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal, and I need to chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n  - **Saffron & Sage** — the Arabic proofs from Priya still need my sign-off.\n  - Confirming my return flight.\n- Housekeeping: clearing a backlog of test noise out of my mail and calendar.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes on what I cut: no counts of unread mail or event noise (reads as a system problem, not yours), and no mention of the drive duplication or the newsletter pile — those are decisions about your own setup, not status. If you''d rather a version that flags the drive question to whoever manages your infrastructure, say so and I''ll rewrite it for that audience.","createdAt":1794332485173}],"content":"Here''s a paste-ready version — trimmed to the things a colleague needs to know, with the workspace-hygiene detail collapsed to one line:\n\n---\n\n**Week of 9–15 Nov**\n\n- In Tokyo through the 15th, back at my desk Monday the 16th.\n- Calendar is clear apart from the daily standup (18:00 JST this week). Nothing else on.\n- Mail''s been quiet since late September, so I''m using the week to close out what''s open:\n  - Six drafts I wrote mid-September and never sent. Going out this week, starting with the **Nov 26 terms**.\n  - **Aozora** — I owe Kenji a reply on the brand proposal, and I need to chase the Harbour Hall hold for the launch venue.\n  - **Saffron & Sage** — the Arabic proofs from Priya still need my sign-off.\n  - Confirming my return flight.\n- Housekeeping: clearing a backlog of test noise out of my mail and calendar.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes on what I cut: no counts of unread mail or event noise (reads as a system problem, not yours), and no mention of the drive duplication or the newsletter pile — those are decisions about your own setup, not status. If you''d rather a version that flags the drive question to whoever manages your infrastructure, say so and I''ll rewrite it for that audience.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T17:41:25.173Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
